{"body":{"from":[{"$ref":"1M6YBY3G0001ZM6"},{"$ref":"1M6YBY3G0001ZQM"},{"$ref":"1M6YBY3G0002072"}],"opens":"The store stays in git, as the site publishes its field as it stands, but not as one loose file per object, which grows with every holon, nor as one file, which every publish rewrites: as packs that never change, one per commit, each holding only what that commit adds, with an index read by range from any static host; growth linear in what changes, and the first birth itself cut into commits at a realistic fidelity, since the whole is structural and its evolution topologically divisible. Files divide two ways: by ownership and wholeness, a store per whole, branch as store; and by time, a pack per commit. What may need forgetting is kept as a store of its own, apart from git until sure; a store can always be picked up, left, worked on and come back to. The birth from markdown may end here: the holons are the source now, and any birth after only produces diff-packs. Git is the carrier of the store's files, never its model.","restsOn":["the file backend writing packs and their indexes","store.md and remotes.md rewritten for packs","glass not based on git, the author's of 2026-11-01"],"stands":"noted","title":"The store packed, carried by git"},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001XF4","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000007"]}
